{
  "about": "Display helper and inject-display messages. engine/src/helper is the reference; its tests, native/macos/tests/DisplayHelperFixtureTests.swift and display-packets.json replay this file. json is the exact line or packet payload. from names who writes it: app is the desktop runtime, macos and windows the helpers. Channels: startup, control, cursor and viewer_input are helper stdout packet kinds 0, 2, 3 and 4; screen is `screen` output; source_stdin is a source's JSON lines and viewer_control kind 2 packets to a viewer; status and control_ready are input helper lines; inject_display_target is the inject-display argument for the binding and target below, answered by inject_display_ready, and each envelope line by inject_display_applied. Whatever Rust writes (from app or windows) must re-encode to the same bytes; macOS key order varies, so its messages only have to parse. The macOS messages were recorded from the helpers' code (ViewerInputModel, DisplayInputTarget, CursorCaptureGeometry) or copied from their literal strings; app and Windows bytes are those of the hand-built messages the typed module replaced. Messages marked ignored are types the app skips.",
